> f(x: u8) = x % 0
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires 0 != 0  (in x % 0)
  defined at 0 of 256 points
  empty domain: undefined at every point of the parameter types
  undefined e.g. at x=0; x=1; x=2; x=3
  C undefined behaviour at 256 points, e.g. x=0
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> u8:
  empty (undefined everywhere)
  undefined at 256 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> equiv f f
f and f: vacuously equal: the domain has no points to compare
